WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.622
A secure XML processing baseline for .

2
00:00:02.622 --> 00:00:11.109
NET applications starts by treating external XML as untrusted unless the application has a verified reason to do otherwise.

3
00:00:11.109 --> 00:00:22.632
The source of a document, the transport channel, or the partner name does not remove the need for controlled parsing, validation, resource limits, and business review.

4
00:00:22.632 --> 00:00:24.909
Configure XML parsers explicitly.

5
00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:39.814
Decide which parser fits the workflow, define DTD behavior, control resolver behavior, set size and entity-related limits where appropriate, and avoid scattered parser construction that depends on uncertain defaults.

6
00:00:39.814 --> 00:00:43.471
Make exceptions rare, documented, and easy to review.

7
00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:47.335
Use trusted schemas and controlled validation contracts.

8
00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:51.889
Keep schemas versioned, reviewed, and deployed from known sources.

9
00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:58.237
Do not let an untrusted document decide where the application retrieves validation material.

10
00:00:58.237 --> 00:01:06.172
Remember that schema validation improves structure checks, but it does not replace authorization or business rules.

11
00:01:06.172 --> 00:01:09.691
Keep query and transformation behavior constrained.

12
00:01:09.691 --> 00:01:13.693
Avoid building XPath expressions directly from user input.

13
00:01:13.693 --> 00:01:17.557
Map user choices to predefined selectors where possible.

14
00:01:17.557 --> 00:01:29.701
Treat XSLT stylesheets as code-like input, use trusted stylesheets, and restrict external resource access and optional transformation features unless they are clearly required.

15
00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:33.151
Finally, handle trust and operations deliberately.

16
00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:37.567
Verify XML signatures only as part of a clear business decision.

17
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.154
Redact logs and errors.

18
00:01:39.154 --> 00:01:46.814
Monitor parse failures, oversized documents, validation drift, transformation failures, and signature failures.

19
00:01:46.814 --> 00:01:54.197
Review production XML workflows as complete systems, from upload and parsing to downstream business action.
